{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-28T13:31:46.012Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"39f0409326ff3a93bdf4de17","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.332","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1791"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1791: several paths after one --add on pm files/docs/test fail with a generic usage error that names neither the repeat-flag fix nor a retry"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"GitHub report https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1791. Reproduced on 2026.11.27 in a sandbox tracker: pm files <id> --add a.ts b.ts c.ts exits 2 with code invalid_command_usage, required 'Use the command with valid arguments and options.' and no suggested retry; the JSON envelope has detail (Commander's message) but no recovery.suggested_retry. pm docs behaves the same. pm test already has targeted guidance (linked_test_value_not_quoted) for an unquoted command split by the shell, which is a different shape. A variadic --add <value...> would swallow an item id written after the flag (pm files --add a.ts <id> is valid today), so the safe fix is a targeted refusal: when every extra positional directly follows a repeatable flag's value and the item id is the first operand, name the repeat-flag fix in the first line and give the exact rewritten command (one --add per value, or --add-glob) in text and in recovery.suggested_retry / suggested_retry_args. Duplicate check: searched repeated --add several paths, too many arguments collection guidance; the transposed 'add' subcommand and linked-resource positional guidance cover other shapes, no item covers this one."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","cli","error-guidance","gh:1791","linked-resources"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-28T13:31:46.012Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-28T13:31:46.012Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":120},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"pm files <id> --add a b c and pm docs <id> --add a b c fail with a targeted code whose first text line names the repeat-flag fix and whose recovery carries the exact retry with one --add per value; pm test <id> --add with several complete entry values gets the same retry, and an unquoted command split by the shell keeps linked_test_value_not_quoted; Repeated --add, --add-glob and an item id written after the flag behave exactly as today, and a positional that does not follow a repeatable flag keeps its current guidance; The suggested retry, replayed in a sandbox, links every value"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-mpbb"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":85},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Several values after one --add are refused with the exact repeated-flag retry in text and JSON"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-28T13:31:46.012Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Duplicate check: searched 'repeated --add several paths one flag usage error' and collection-guidance terms; no open or closed item owns extra values after one --add. Filed from GH-1791 on 2026-11-28."}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"724bb1