{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-28T14:45:18.441Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"39f0409326ff3a93bdf4de17","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-928ng6","lineage:pm-928ng6","lineage:pm-u9d0","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"pm-928ng6","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-928ng6","lineage:pm-928ng6","lineage:pm-u9d0","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.332","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-28T14:45:18.440Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Codex review round 1 (2026-11-28), three P2 findings, all valid and fixed. (1) Colon-form entries: path:a,note:fix the bug got an executable retry because only = marked a value as structured. Values are now judged by the artifact parser's own looksLikeStructuredPathEntry and parse functions (parseAddEntries, parseAddGlobEntries, parseRemoveEntries, parseMigrateEntries): a mix of structured and bare values, or a value the parser refuses, gets the quoting hint and no retry. (2) Ancestor options: pm files --json <id> --add a b got the generic error, and pm files <id> --add --json a b took --json as the value of --add. The resolver now classifies the tokens Commander sees, with global options stripped by the bootstrap's own globalBootstrapTokenSpan, which stripGlobalBootstrapTokens now also reads, and maps each insertion back to its argv position. (3) Linked-test entries: path= alone, cmd= for --remove and 0 for --remove-index got a retry. sdk/test/execution.ts now exports admitsLinkedTestFlagValue, which calls the flag's own parser (parseAddEntry, parseAddJsonEntries, parseRemoveEntries, parseRemoveIndexes, parseTestRunMeasurements). Also caught by the full suite: the module had statically pulled registration-helpers (commander) and the parsers into error-guidance, which is on the boot path, so pm --version without runtime dependencies failed. commander-usage now resolves the recovery asynchronously with a dynamic import, only for a too-many-arguments refusal, and error-guidance only formats the result."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-28T14:45:18.441Z"}],"before_hash":"bbfa9723e8db4cfbae78d716ee2cc627967485eab77ea537c06f4334719dc8cd","after_hash":"55f715b69ddd886fadda1625ff28f686bdc1931ac5d6d54c2f1ff7f10ed73174","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"7b80430b4e89105484b04d08dc2e77cb077abfc61da0ab67572f92102fd0ff71"}
