{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-28T15:35:35.212Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"39f0409326ff3a93bdf4de17","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.332","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-28T15:35:35.211Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Codex review round 2, 2026-11-28: two P2 findings and one P3, all valid, settled by principle. (1) Token ownership: the root program declares every global option to Commander (sdk/cli-program.ts), so the command's arity table, which walks to the root, is the whole parse. The round-1 bootstrap strip was the wrong model: pm files <id> --output-limit --add a b got a retry that failed again, because Commander gives --add to --output-limit. The scan now uses the table alone, the first operand is the id, and any other operand must directly follow a repeatable flag's value chain; the globalBootstrapTokenSpan refactor was reverted. (2) Exactness: --add-glob pattern:src,note:fix the bug and docs --add Release notes,https://example.org got retries that change the mutation. An executable retry now requires PLAIN values (no whitespace, comma, = or :, and not option-like) that the flag's parser accepts. Every structured value gets the quoting hint without a retry. Real-CLI cases are covered. (3) P3: --remove command:a now replays, because the selector check accepts : as well as =, as parseRemoveEntries does."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-28T15:35:35.212Z"}],"before_hash":"5db21431553c9c59dd3564e3fb948afa9c37b1afce890c1ba41cf6b96fe39e0e","after_hash":"d1d627f44397dd59420c34ce608a38bcb5ae944088dfa2b06fa3d7b9e080d494","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"f4f73e52564c76c7647e170b59566f56b354a7b4aa460cc19a15f3f33b303490"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-28T16:04:41.011Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"39f0409326ff3a93bdf4de17","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.332","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/4","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-28T16:04:41.010Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Codex review round 3, 2026-11-28. Two fixed: (a) a required option value that reads as an option is where Commander's ancestor-first parse can disagree with a flat scan (pm files <id> --message --json --add a b gives --json to the program), so readOptionToken now claims no span there and the recovery declines; (b) an operand naming a subcommand of the invoked command (files --note N discover ...) means the subcommand refused, so the scan declines. Two declined, with reason (settled principle: the executable retry corrects only the value-list shape): an unrelated invalid value kept in the retry (--migrate bogus) and --measure without --run each surface their own native refusal on replay, which is the correct next error. Inventing --run would execute linked commands."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-28T16:04:41.011Z"}],"before_hash":"d1d627f44397dd59420c34ce608a38bcb5ae944088dfa2b06fa3d7b9e080d494","after_hash":"d6adced7ed636de72c935e94187319f61ac02ff939ddafbfaaee5f7e6e16eb70","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"f0ae077c8e33a5ec46073008f143ddb80f870d8ad39bbf3e73c37589225ad30f"}
